## ✅ Rebuilt — Two paths, compound condition

The logic is now exactly what you described: **both flags must be true at the same time** to trigger the escalation path. Everything else — urgent but not VIP, VIP but not urgent, neither — takes the ticket path.

### How it works now

```
Email Received
    ↓
Classify Email  ──── sets isUrgent (true/false) AND isVip (true/false) independently
    ↓
VIP + Urgent?  ── expression: isUrgent === true && isVip === true
   ↙ true                                    ↘ false
Alert: Urgent (Slack)               Create Support Ticket
Reply to Customer (urgent reply)    Reply: Ticket Created (with TKT-ref)
→ Escalated (End)                   → Ticket Created (End)
```

**The "both true" path** fires the Slack alert and the immediate personal reply.  
**Everything else** — any single-flag case or neither — goes straight to ticket + auto-reply.

### Two things to still customize

| Item | What to do |
|---|---|
| **VIP domains** | In `classifyEmail1`, replace `['enterprise.com', 'bigclient.io', 'premiumcorp.net']` with your real customer domains |
| **Slack channel** | `alertUrgent1` currently posts to channel `C01H4SPS77W` — update to whichever channel your team actually monitors for escalations |

